      "content": "13.1 Traditional Sports"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Kalaripayattu is one of the oldest traditional martial art forms in the world, originating in Kerala.",
        "Vallam Kali (Snake Boat Race), particularly the Nehru Trophy Boat Race at Punnamada Lake, is a major traditional sport.",
        "Kerala has a rich sporting heritage, producing elite international athletes such as P.T. Usha, M.D. Valsamma, and Jimmy George.",
        "The state possesses robust sports infrastructure managed under the umbrella of the Kerala State Sports Council."
      ],
